<title>LATVIA: Latvian central bank issues licence to new bank.</title>
<headline>Latvian central bank issues licence to new bank.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's central bank said in a statement on Friday that it had issued a licence to a new bank, Maras Bank.</p>
<p>The central bank said that the new bank had 3.5 million lats in capital.</p>
<p>Latvia now has 34 licensed banks in its banking sector, which is recovering from a crisis sparked late last year by the surprise closure of the country's largest bank, Banka Baltija.</p>
<p>--Riga newsroom +371 721 52 40</p>
</text>
